    "end": "Ian's still walking back.",
    "caption": "Pip has done this walk before.\n\nWalkies: 2.1 million people, about four million dogs, a 25-hour day, two moons, and a dog walk that goes as far as the dog would like: three deserts, a red one, a stony one and a frozen one, then home for tea. Dogs do it before lunch. People take a flask, spare socks and, if they're sensible, the bus fare back.\n\nI borrowed a spaniel for the afternoon. I got as far as the stony one, and she sent a postcard.\n\n(The largest desert on Earth is Antarctica. A desert is about how little falls from the sky, not how hot it is. On Walkies, it's the spaniels' favourite.)\n\nHow many deserts would yours do before tea?"
  },
  "first_comment": "Ian's wife walks Pip now. She takes the car.",
